{#
  The three duty states of one member on one day, as three full-width
  buttons labelled in words.

  It replaced a single button cycling ✓ → ✗ → — with no legend anywhere:
  three glyphs, three meanings, and no way to reach a state except by
  pressing through the others. Naming them is also what lets the phone
  layout drop the colour-only coding the desktop grid uses.

  Used twice, and the second use is why `date` may be empty: the day sheet
  renders ONE copy of the roster for the whole month and
  public/assets/js/sos-admin.js stamps `data-date` on it when a day is
  opened. `.sos-state-button[data-member-id][data-date][data-state]` is
  the contract that file grips (the desktop grid keeps its own
  `.sos-oncall-cell` cells, and both are repainted from one place).

  Usage:
  {% include '@sos_staff/partials/state_buttons.html.twig' with {
      member_id: 42,
      date: '2026-06-15',        -- '' in the day sheet, stamped by JS
      state: 'oncall',           -- 'oncall' | 'unavailable' | null
      group_label: 'État de Akela',
  } only %}

  Height comes from `.tap-target` in app.css's `pointer: coarse` block
  (design.md §7.2), never from an inline min-height.

  The three buttons are grouped by a real <fieldset> rather than by a
  generic element carrying role="group": the <legend> names the group for
  screen readers exactly as the former aria-label did, and Bootstrap's
  reboot strips the fieldset's border, padding and margin, so the visible
  rendering is the .btn-group row alone. The row keeps `mt-2` itself
  rather than handing it to the fieldset — a block-level margin there
  would collapse with the preceding heading's and close the gap. The
  legend is `.visually-hidden` because the group is already named on
  screen by the day heading (phone list) or the member's name (day
  sheet).
#}
<fieldset>
    <legend class="visually-hidden">{{ group_label }}</legend>
    <div class="btn-group w-100 mt-2">
        <button type="button"
                class="btn btn-sm tap-target sos-state-button {{ state == 'oncall' ? 'btn-success' : 'btn-outline-secondary' }}"
                data-member-id="{{ member_id }}" data-date="{{ date }}" data-state="oncall"
                aria-pressed="{{ state == 'oncall' ? 'true' : 'false' }}">Garde</button>
        <button type="button"
                class="btn btn-sm tap-target sos-state-button {{ state == 'unavailable' ? 'btn-danger' : 'btn-outline-secondary' }}"
                data-member-id="{{ member_id }}" data-date="{{ date }}" data-state="unavailable"
                aria-pressed="{{ state == 'unavailable' ? 'true' : 'false' }}">Indispo</button>
        <button type="button"
                class="btn btn-sm tap-target sos-state-button {{ state ? 'btn-outline-secondary' : 'btn-secondary' }}"
                data-member-id="{{ member_id }}" data-date="{{ date }}" data-state=""
                aria-pressed="{{ state ? 'false' : 'true' }}">Rien</button>
    </div>
</fieldset>
